# Line endings, pinned where they actually matter.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows and built into a Linux container. Git's
# default on Windows checks files out with CRLF, which is harmless for Python
# but not for files a Linux shell reads literally: a trailing \r ends up inside
# the command a `RUN` or `CMD` executes, producing errors that name a command
# with an invisible character appended to it.
#
# `text=auto` lets git normalise text files to LF in the repository while
# leaving the working copy alone; the explicit `eol=lf` entries force the
# checked-out file to LF as well, on every platform.
* text=auto

Dockerfile   text eol=lf
.dockerignore text eol=lf
*.sh         text eol=lf

# Checkpoints are binary; never let a line-ending filter near one.
*.pt binary
